# License and third-party terms

This repository is released for **non-commercial research and evaluation use only**.

The reason is inherited, not chosen: the Gaussian-splatting rasterizer this code
builds on (`submodules/diff-gaussian-rasterization`) is distributed by Inria and
the Max Planck Institute for Informatics under the *Gaussian-Splatting License*,
which grants non-exclusive rights "for research purposes" and permits use
"non-commercially, i.e., for research and/or evaluation purposes only".

## What this means for you

- **Academic and industrial research use is permitted**, free of charge.
- **Commercial use is not permitted** without a separate license from Inria/MPII.
- You may reproduce, prepare derivative works, and redistribute the software for
  research purposes, provided you keep this notice and the upstream licenses
  intact. There is no right to sublicense.
- This repository's own code (everything not under `submodules/`) is offered to
  you under the same non-commercial research terms, so that the combined work
  has a single, honest license statement.

## Upstream components and their licenses

| Component | Location | License |
|---|---|---|
| Gaussian-splatting rasterizer | `submodules/diff-gaussian-rasterization` | Inria/MPII Gaussian-Splatting License (non-commercial research); full text in that directory's `LICENSE.md` |
| `simple-knn` | `submodules/simple-knn` | Inria/MPII Gaussian-Splatting License (same terms) |
| MonoGS (upstream platform) | derived, see `PROVENANCE.md` | Inria/MPII Gaussian-Splatting License |
| Mask R-CNN weights | downloaded at runtime via torchvision | TorchVision / Meta research-only terms; see the torchvision model license |
| RAFT optical-flow weights | downloaded at runtime via `torch.hub` | BSD-3-Clause (princeton-vl/RAFT) |
| Bonn RGB-D Dynamic dataset | downloaded by `scripts/download_bonn.sh` | CC BY 4.0 (University of Bonn); cite the ReFusion/BoT-SORT papers |
| TUM RGB-D dataset | downloaded by `scripts/download_tum.sh` | CC BY 4.0 (TU Munich) |

